INT. CHINESE RESTAURANT BACK ROOM, MAH-JONG TABLE - NIGHT

Cigarette haze. A round table. Six men and women, tiles clacking.

MADAME LOTUS FONG-ADEWALE (60s) sits at the head, perfectly still. To her left, VINNIE "THE CLERK" CARUSO-OBI (50s) shuffles. Beside him, DOLLY ZHAO-HARTLEY (40s) files her nails. Across, BIG MOSES TEMPLETON-AGYEMAN (50s), enormous, sweating. Next to him, QUINCY PARK-DELGADO (30s), tapping a tile. And the last, FATHER PASCAL EZEKWESILI-MORROW (60s, collar loose), stares at his hand.

The tiles click. Click. Click.

MADAME LOTUS
(not looking up)
Someone here has been talking.

Nobody moves. Dolly's nail file stops. Moses lifts a tile, sets it down. Quincy's hand slides from the table to his lap.

VINNIE
Madame --

MADAME LOTUS ^
Vincent. Not you.

She picks up a tile, turns it over, and sets it face-up on the felt. It's blank. She waits.

Father Pascal reaches into his coat. Every head swivels. He draws out a rosary and kisses it.

The tiles click again.
